{{Term/Store|Shard of Farosh's Fang|Shards of Farosh's Fang|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Shard of Farosh's Fang}}<br/>This shard fell from the golden spirit Farosh's fang. It's so hard, hammers bounce right off it, so it's impossible to process. Yet rumors say it does have some use as a material.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Shard of Farosh's Fang}}<br/>An extremely hard chip of one of Farosh's fangs. Attach it to a weapon to greatly increase its attack power. It can also be used in cooking.|Inventory|TotK}}</ref>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Shards of Farosh's Fang are acquired by shooting the dragon [[Farosh]] in the lower mouth. The spot it was shot will glow, and the Shard will fall to the ground. Farosh can be found flying through [[Lake Hylia]], [[Lake Floria]], and the [[Gerudo Highlands]]. If Shards of Farosh's Fang are used in a [[Cooking Pot]], the resulting meal will always be [[Dubious Food]]. The Shards can also be used as an ingredient to make Light Yellow [[Dye]] at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] in [[Hateno Village]].

Shards of Farosh's Fang are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Shard of Farosh's Fang}}

